 DeepSeek `site:` filters. Queries are limited to DeepSeek's 128-character
 limit; `max_uses` is capped at 64 per request (default 8).
 
-Set `HIPFIRE_DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` in the HipFire server process environment
-(`DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` is accepted as a fallback). Because this enables paid
-search using a server-held credential, the HipFire listener must also have
-`serve.api_key_file` configured; requests without a valid bearer are already
-rejected before the request body is read. The direct Search API is billed per
-successful result; see [DeepSeek Search & Fetch billing](https://api-docs.deepseek.com/guides/search/#billing).
+Configure the server-owned key with HipFire's typed config commands:
+
+```bash
+hipfire config set serve.deepseek_api_key_file /absolute/path/to/deepseek-api-key
+hipfire config set serve.deepseek_search_url https://api.deepseek.com/v1/tools/search
+hipfire config explain serve.deepseek_api_key_file
+```
+
+The credential file follows the existing `serve.api_key_file` rules: at least
+32 printable ASCII bytes, with Unix permissions granting no group/other access
+(`chmod 600`). Configuration and diagnostics contain its path, never its value.
+The service loads it at startup; restart serve after changing either the path,
+file contents, or endpoint. An empty path disables native web search.
+
+Client `X-HipFire-DeepSeek-API-Key` headers and the old `HIPFIRE_DEEPSEEK_API_KEY`
+/ `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` environment variables are ignored. Ordinary server bearer
+authentication remains optional and follows the existing `serve.api_key_file`
+setting. All callers allowed to use this server share its search credential and
+quota. The endpoint must use HTTPS, except loopback mock servers; redirects are
+disabled. Search uses the provider's billed API; see
+[DeepSeek Search & Fetch billing](https://api-docs.deepseek.com/guides/search/#billing).
 
 Dynamic filtering that calls web search from `code_execution` is refused unless
 the tool explicitly permits direct calls. The Search API accepts an IP address
